{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — I have already explained it, for it is an abbreviated form, and thus it is: יהוה אלהי צבאות (YHWH, God of hosts)." "And the meaning of \"hosts\" — the angels, and corresponding to them Jacob was mentioned, for his sons are His hosts on earth, as in: כל צבאות ה' (all the hosts of YHWH). And this psalmist prays to bring about salvation. And the correct interpretation: it is joined with the verse after it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 84, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The Hebrew quotes יהוה אלהי צבאות but the full phrase he refers to in the verse is יהוה אלהים אלהי צבאות; the shorter quotation may reflect his abbreviating or a variant reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:01.990096528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}